1. Introduction

1.1 Purpose

The purpose of the School Result Management System (SRMS) is to allow administrators to record student details, enter subject scores, and view results in a structured, accurate, and efficient manner.

1.2 Scope

SRMS is a console-based Python application that can:
	•	Add new students
	•	Add subjects
	•	Record student scores
	•	View the results of a student
	•	List all students
	•	Provide simple result management for schools

The system uses a simple SQLite database for storing all details permanently.

1.3 Definitions
	•	SRMS – School Result Management System
	•	Admin – User controlling the system
	•	Student – A person whose records are stored in the system


2. Overall Description

2.1 Product Perspective

The system is standalone, running on Python. It consists of:
	•	A database module (srms_db.py)
	•	A console UI (srms_console.py)

2.2 Product Functions

The SRMS will provide the following functions:
Add Student
Add Subject
Record Score
View Result
List Students

3. System Requirements

3.1 Functional Requirements

FR1: Add Student
	•	The system shall allow the admin to register a new student with student_id and student_name.

FR2: Add Subject
	•	The system shall allow the admin to create new subjects.

FR3: Record Score
	•	The system shall allow input of a score between 0 and 100.
	•	The system shall link the score with a student and a subject.

FR4: View Student Result
	•	The system shall display all subjects and corresponding scores for a student.

FR5: List Students
	•	The system shall show all students stored in the system.

3.2 Non-Functional Requirements

NFR1: Usability
	•	Simple, clear console menu.

NFR2: Reliability
	•	Data is stored in SQLite to ensure persistence.

NFR3: Performance
	•	System must load responses within 2 seconds for all operations.

NFR4: Maintainability
	•	Python modules use modular structure for easier editing.

4. System Design

4.1 Modules
	1.	srms_db.py
	•	Handles database operations
	•	Creates tables
	•	Inserts students, subjects, and scores
	•	Fetches results
	2.	srms_console.py
	•	User Interface
	•	Menu options
	•	Interacts with SRMSDB class

5. Constraints
	•	Python 3.7+
	•	sqlite3 library

6. Conclusion

This SRS outlines all requirements for the School Result Management System and guides the implementation process to ensure consistency between design and code.

